<article class="env-remark" id="0FEL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FEL">Remark <span data-tag="0FEL">42.56.4</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$ be locally of finite type over $S$. The Chern class map defines a canonical map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  c : K_0(\textit{Vect}(X)) \longrightarrow \prod \nolimits _{i \geq 0} A^ i(X)  \]
</div>
  <p> by sending a generator $[\mathcal{E}]$ on the left hand side to $c(\mathcal{E}) = 1 + c_1(\mathcal{E}) + c_2(\mathcal{E}) + \ldots $ and extending multiplicatively. Thus $-[\mathcal{E}]$ is sent to the formal inverse $c(\mathcal{E})^{-1}$ which is why we have the infinite product on the right hand side. This is well defined by Lemma <a href="/tag/02UI" data-tag="02UI">42.40.3</a>. </p>
</article>